/A 2557 0 R
/Alt (Flowchart of a pipeline optimization model showing inputs, model structure, and outputs. Inputs include source set, sink set, candidate arcs, pipeline diameters, planning periods, and uncertain scenarios. The optimization model involves decision variables such as pipeline construction and CO2 flow allocation, aims to minimize total discounted system cost, considers constraints like mass balance and storage capacity, and includes features such as MILP and robust optimization. Outputs are pipeline layout, optimal diameters, CO2 flow schedule, expansion pathway, and cost-risk performance.)
